<title>UK: FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Consensus on UK company results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Analysts' estimates of UK company results expected in week ending May 9 include -</p>
<p>COMPANY----------------PFT/DIV/EPS--CONSENSUS----RANGE---------PS</p>
<p>MONDAY, May 5</p>
<p>No major companies reporting results</p>
<p>TUESDAY, May 6</p>
<p>British Petroleum Plc   *1Q  PFT     691.5    657.0-725.0  633.0</p>
<p>				     DIV	 5.25	 5.25	4.25</p>
<p>WEDNESDAY, May 7</p>
<p>BSkyB Plc		    3Q  PFT	80.4     75.0-85.0  71.2</p>
<p>Royal Bank of Scotland  **H  PFT     363.3    345.0-383.0 301.0</p>
<p>				     DIV	 6.2     6.05-6.2     5.4</p>
<p>J. Sainsbury Plc	    F  PFT     644.0    640.0-650.0 764.0</p>
<p>				     DIV	12.1     12.1-12.4   12.1</p>
<p>				     EPS	23.0     22.7-23.3   26.8</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 645.0 DIV 12.3 EPS 23.2)</p>
<p>Tate &amp; Lyle Plc	     H  PFT     119.6    112.7-129.0 168.2</p>
<p>				     DIV	 5.6	5.3-5.7     5.3</p>
<p>				     EPS	16.2     15.5-17.5   23.0</p>
<p>Whitbread Plc		 F  PFT     316.6    313.0-321.0 285.7</p>
<p>				     DIV	23.8     23.5-24.0  21.85</p>
<p>				     EPS	48.0     46.7-48.8  43.25</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 318.0 DIV 23.75 EPS 48.5)</p>
<p>THURSDAY, May 8</p>
<p>Body Shop Plc		 F  PFT	37.7     36.5-39.0   32.7</p>
<p>				     DIV	 4.5	4.1-5.0     3.4</p>
<p>				     EPS	11.7     11.2-12.0   10.0</p>
<p>(Edinburgh Financial Publishing's estimate directory shows a consensus forecast of PFT 37.5 DIV 4.5 EPS 11.6)</p>
<p>Kwik Save Group Plc	 H  PFT	36.8     43.0-32.0   44.2</p>
<p>				     DIV	 5.95	 5.95	5.95</p>
<p>All profit figures are pretax, exclude exceptional items unless otherwise stated and are in millions stg. Dividends are total net and quoted as pence per share.</p>
<p>* Forecasts on a replacement cost basis before exceptional items</p>
<p>** Forecast includes Citizen's sale of mortgage and investor services to Bank United Corp netting Royal Bank approximately 25 milion stg</p>
<p>-Andrew Langlands, London Newsroom +44 171 542 3496</p>
